.TH iron-vault-config-approve 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-config\-approve \- Propose FILE as the new config: the service shows its summary, asks for confirmation and the approval passphrase, then commits, publishes and activates it. Stdin is not read for the config, because it carries the answers to the prompts when it is not a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault config approve\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Propose FILE as the new config: the service shows its summary, asks for confirmation and the approval passphrase, then commits, publishes and activates it. Stdin is not read for the config, because it carries the answers to the prompts when it is not a terminal
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The proposed config file
